WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.236 --> 00:00:01.920
(Mark laughs)
- [Mark] Rebecca.

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:03.530
- Hi

00:00:03.530 --> 00:00:04.790
- [Mark] how are you?
- I'm good.

00:00:04.790 --> 00:00:05.900
- [Mark] So nice to see you again.

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:06.780
- So nice to see you.

00:00:06.780 --> 00:00:07.960
- [Mark] It's been a long time.

00:00:07.960 --> 00:00:08.793
- Definitely.

00:00:08.793 --> 00:00:09.830
- [Mark] I haven't seen
you in many months.

00:00:09.830 --> 00:00:11.380
- Yeah. How many months has it been?

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:12.213
Like four or five months?

00:00:12.213 --> 00:00:13.069
- [Mark] I bet it's been
four or five months. Yeah.

00:00:13.069 --> 00:00:13.902
- Yeah.

00:00:13.902 --> 00:00:15.240
- [Mark] You doin' all right?
- I'm doing good.

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:16.570
How about you?
- [Mark] I'm doing fine.

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:17.920
What's going on with you?

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:18.753
- Nothing really.

00:00:18.753 --> 00:00:20.970
I was just floating around.

00:00:20.970 --> 00:00:21.830
- [Mark] Where have you been?

00:00:21.830 --> 00:00:23.700
- I've been spending
some time in the Valley

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:25.840
and just kind of running
through the Hills.

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:26.980
You ever heard that song?

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:28.000
I was in Arizona.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:30.610
And there were these pink, fluffy clouds.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:32.260
Just be looking at the sky a lot.

00:00:33.192 --> 00:00:34.025
(Rebecca chuckles)
Sorry.

00:00:34.025 --> 00:00:35.610
- [Mark] Where were you sleeping?

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:36.443
- Anywhere. (chuckles)

00:00:36.443 --> 00:00:38.560
- [Mark] Yeah, just same answer. (laughs)

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:40.463
I'm always concerned about
where you're sleeping.

00:00:41.790 --> 00:00:43.090
And is your life better?

00:00:43.090 --> 00:00:45.750
Is your life worse than
last time I saw you?

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:48.120
- Well, I don't wanna say worse.

00:00:48.120 --> 00:00:50.640
Like I said, I got in this car accident.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:51.770
- [Mark] Tell me about that.

00:00:51.770 --> 00:00:55.550
Well, basically it was just
like, it was really freaky.

00:00:55.550 --> 00:00:56.383
- [Mark] You're walking?

00:00:56.383 --> 00:00:57.610
- So I was walking. Yeah.

00:00:57.610 --> 00:00:59.190
And I was trying to, well,

00:00:59.190 --> 00:01:00.170
really ironically enough,

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:02.370
I just found a whole bag of shoes.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:05.010
And as I'm coming to cross the street,

00:01:05.010 --> 00:01:07.200
cause I left some
cigarettes with my friend

00:01:07.200 --> 00:01:09.490
to give her all these shoes.

00:01:09.490 --> 00:01:10.930
This car just comes out of nowhere.

00:01:10.930 --> 00:01:12.940
All I remember is somersaulting.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:15.940
And then I looked down
and my legs snapped.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:18.930
Then I kept trying to push it back in

00:01:18.930 --> 00:01:20.730
and a (chuckles)

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.600
and it wouldn't, my bone was
completely stumped in half.

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.433
- [Mark] Your leg,

00:01:24.433 --> 00:01:26.530
- Yeah. my right leg.

00:01:26.530 --> 00:01:28.010
- [Mark] Down there.
- Yeah. Got a scar.

00:01:28.010 --> 00:01:30.360
- [Mark] Oh my God. Look at (laughs)

00:01:30.360 --> 00:01:32.905
- I think my scar is the most
beautiful thing about me.

00:01:32.905 --> 00:01:34.440
(Rebecca laughs)

00:01:34.440 --> 00:01:37.090
- [Mark] There's a lot of
beautiful things about you.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:39.430
But you've healed?

00:01:39.430 --> 00:01:41.653
- Yeah. There's pins in my legs.

00:01:42.600 --> 00:01:43.551
- [Mark] You have pins in your legs.

00:01:43.551 --> 00:01:44.540
- (murmurs)

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:45.400
Was it painful?

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.870
No.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:48.880
It hurts sometimes, but, the surgery,

00:01:48.880 --> 00:01:49.980
I didn't feel a thing.

00:01:51.450 --> 00:01:52.773
It hurts to walk though.

00:01:55.020 --> 00:01:56.640
- [Mark] But you're surviving.

00:01:56.640 --> 00:01:57.473
- Thriving.

00:01:57.473 --> 00:01:59.690
- [Mark] You're thriving.
(Rebecca laughs)

00:01:59.690 --> 00:02:00.883
You seem a little more,

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:06.230
less out of your mind than some
of the other visits you've,

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:07.410
- Yeah.
- [Mark] Grace me with that.

00:02:07.410 --> 00:02:08.740
- Maybe more like,

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:09.810
- [Mark] You seem a little more grounded.

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:12.480
- Composed. Yeah.
- [Mark] Yeah. Why is that?

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.313
- I don't know.

00:02:13.313 --> 00:02:15.170
I guess I've just been meditating more.

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:17.820
I've just been more relaxed lately.

00:02:17.820 --> 00:02:18.680
Less frenetic.

00:02:18.680 --> 00:02:19.770
I don't know.

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:21.590
I guess the seasons,

00:02:21.590 --> 00:02:22.423
I feel like,

00:02:22.423 --> 00:02:26.030
I don't know, what this
epidemic or, sorry, pandemic.

00:02:26.030 --> 00:02:27.480
- [Mark] Yes.

00:02:27.480 --> 00:02:29.170
- Everything's so much more relaxed.

00:02:29.170 --> 00:02:31.181
So I'm just wandering
streets more at night.

00:02:31.181 --> 00:02:33.730
More taking long walks.

00:02:33.730 --> 00:02:36.250
Then I am like, partying.

00:02:36.250 --> 00:02:38.513
- [Mark] Is COVID effecting you?

00:02:38.513 --> 00:02:40.630
- Yes and no.

00:02:40.630 --> 00:02:42.173
I feel like I'm kind of,

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:44.900
I don't know how to put it.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:47.253
COVID proves that the system works.

00:02:48.790 --> 00:02:51.440
Everyone just bought into
it automatically like that.

00:02:52.460 --> 00:02:54.020
I don't know how I feel

00:02:54.020 --> 00:02:55.700
about being on the fringe anymore

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:56.990
because it makes me feel like so much more

00:02:56.990 --> 00:02:58.430
of an outcast.

00:02:58.430 --> 00:03:00.890
Because I'm not in the fervor

00:03:01.740 --> 00:03:02.910
of it.

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:03.743
I don't,

00:03:03.743 --> 00:03:04.770
- [Mark] You're not running around scared.

00:03:04.770 --> 00:03:07.570
I'm not scared because
there was swine flu,

00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:08.490
there was bird flu.

00:03:08.490 --> 00:03:10.250
I feel like fear feeds fear.

00:03:10.250 --> 00:03:11.083
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:11.083 --> 00:03:12.480
- You know, we have nothing
to fear but fear itself.

00:03:12.480 --> 00:03:14.230
- [Mark] But there are
people dying from it.

00:03:14.230 --> 00:03:16.000
- It's awful, unfortunately.

00:03:16.000 --> 00:03:17.370
- [Mark] Somewhere, hospitals where,

00:03:17.370 --> 00:03:20.646
- [Mark] There are people
dying of starvation all over.

00:03:20.646 --> 00:03:23.115
(Rebecca laughs)

00:03:23.115 --> 00:03:24.400
Have you talked with your family at all?

00:03:24.400 --> 00:03:25.630
- No.
- [Mark] No.

00:03:25.630 --> 00:03:28.453
- No. I barely got to hold on to a phone.

00:03:29.462 --> 00:03:31.270
- [Mark] Oh.
- Yeah.

00:03:31.270 --> 00:03:32.410
- [Mark] Do you have friends?

00:03:32.410 --> 00:03:33.243
- I have friends. Yeah.

00:03:33.243 --> 00:03:34.700
- [Mark] You do. So you're not lonely.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:36.350
- I'm not lonely.

00:03:36.350 --> 00:03:37.720
- [Mark] You're just drifting around and,

00:03:37.720 --> 00:03:39.160
- Yeah. I like doing that.

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:40.570
I don't know why I like doing it.

00:03:40.570 --> 00:03:42.230
- [Mark] Yeah. You're happy.

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:43.250
You seem happy.

00:03:43.250 --> 00:03:45.470
- Yeah. But I feel like I
need to judge myself for it.

00:03:45.470 --> 00:03:46.470
I don't.

00:03:46.470 --> 00:03:49.310
It's so convenient when it's just me.

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:51.843
It's the minute I have to
give it a context, you know?

00:03:53.140 --> 00:03:54.640
- [Mark] But you like this
life of no responsibility?

00:03:54.640 --> 00:03:57.423
- I do. I hate that I
love it so much but I do.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:02.890
- [Mark] You think you've
gained some weight?

00:04:02.890 --> 00:04:05.070
- Yeah. A little bit.

00:04:05.070 --> 00:04:06.370
Cause they had me in physical therapy

00:04:06.370 --> 00:04:08.020
so I was like laying in bed for a month.

00:04:08.020 --> 00:04:08.890
- [Mark] Oh, that'll do it.

00:04:08.890 --> 00:04:10.347
- Yeah.

00:04:10.347 --> 00:04:11.583
- [Mark] I like your outfit.
- Thank you.

00:04:11.583 --> 00:04:13.150
- [Mark] Where'd you get
them? Where'd you find them?

00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:14.325
- Found it on the floor.

00:04:14.325 --> 00:04:15.510
(Mark laughs)

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:17.080
- I found this on the floor

00:04:17.080 --> 00:04:18.640
and I found this,

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:20.450
it was just sitting there on a bridge.

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:23.970
I had it like a cloak, like
I had it like a druid cloak.

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:26.640
And then I turned it and
burned it into a skirt.

00:04:26.640 --> 00:04:27.473
- [Mark] You sure did.

00:04:27.473 --> 00:04:28.625
You always come up with
something creative.

00:04:28.625 --> 00:04:31.460
(Rebecca laughs)

00:04:31.460 --> 00:04:33.750
So what's your plan for the holidays?

00:04:33.750 --> 00:04:34.600
- I have no idea.

00:04:35.690 --> 00:04:36.593
No idea.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:40.960
You don't really celebrate
holidays very often

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:41.990
living the way I do. You know what I mean?

00:04:41.990 --> 00:04:43.030
- [Mark] No, you don't.

00:04:43.030 --> 00:04:44.340
- Every day is a celebration.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:45.173
- Every day is,

00:04:45.173 --> 00:04:47.040
(both laughing)

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.160
- Every day is an excuse.

00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:50.570
- [Mark] So you had an auto accident.

00:04:50.570 --> 00:04:51.403
- Yeah.

00:04:51.403 --> 00:04:52.236
- [Mark] What's the best
thing that's happened to you

00:04:52.236 --> 00:04:53.069
since I saw you last?

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.360
- I met this Rockefeller.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:04:59.560
I spent the night with him.

00:04:59.560 --> 00:05:00.940
He was really weird.

00:05:00.940 --> 00:05:03.283
He was really weird, but he was great.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:05.780
I don't know if I wanna
talk about it too much.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:06.613
- [Mark] Don't talk about it too much.

00:05:06.613 --> 00:05:07.520
- It was like one of those
things, you know what I mean?

00:05:07.520 --> 00:05:09.360
Like a conspiracy, like a hush hush thing.

00:05:09.360 --> 00:05:10.550
- [Mark] Yeah. You don't need to,

00:05:10.550 --> 00:05:11.383
- Although, you know,

00:05:11.383 --> 00:05:12.830
- [Mark] We don't need to
get anybody in hot water.

00:05:12.830 --> 00:05:13.663
- Yeah.

00:05:13.663 --> 00:05:15.580
(Rebecca laughs)

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:19.100
- But yeah. Just call him Mr. Rockefeller.

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.690
And he was,

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:23.130
he was very, you know when people,

00:05:23.130 --> 00:05:24.880
I never understood the word visionary

00:05:24.880 --> 00:05:26.300
until I met that person.

00:05:26.300 --> 00:05:27.950
'Cause

00:05:27.950 --> 00:05:28.790
it's like real estate.

00:05:28.790 --> 00:05:31.040
Like I could never understand commodity,

00:05:31.040 --> 00:05:32.890
and this person helped me understand

00:05:35.200 --> 00:05:36.800
what it is to have

00:05:38.070 --> 00:05:39.690
more than you know what to do with.

00:05:39.690 --> 00:05:44.095
And I liked that

00:05:44.095 --> 00:05:47.428
The stuff he said to me was incredible.

00:05:48.990 --> 00:05:50.330
- [Mark] You're learning things?

00:05:50.330 --> 00:05:51.430
You're growing as a person?

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.511
- Yes. Growing from love.

00:05:53.511 --> 00:05:56.300
I can't remember what
that's from. (chuckles)

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:59.703
Yes. I'm a budding blossom
of a beautiful petunia.

00:06:01.540 --> 00:06:02.910
- [Mark] You're certainly interesting.

00:06:02.910 --> 00:06:03.780
- Thank you.

00:06:03.780 --> 00:06:05.780
I get lots of interesting
people in front of my cameras.

00:06:05.780 --> 00:06:08.054
You're somewhere at the top of the list.

00:06:08.054 --> 00:06:09.460
(Rebecca laughs)

00:06:09.460 --> 00:06:10.500
- I don't believe that for a second.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:13.860
I've seen some of the people,
I found your page finally.

00:06:13.860 --> 00:06:15.860
I think the people that you
find it very interesting.

00:06:15.860 --> 00:06:16.693
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:06:16.693 --> 00:06:17.526
- I feel like I'm quite down,

00:06:17.526 --> 00:06:18.359
- [Mark] I'm really lucky.
- Yeah.

00:06:18.359 --> 00:06:20.038
[Mark]Did you watch your videos?

00:06:20.038 --> 00:06:20.871
- I did. Yeah.

00:06:20.871 --> 00:06:23.440
- [Mark] What do you think of yourself?

00:06:23.440 --> 00:06:26.560
- I am strange. (chuckles)

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:27.450
I like it though.

00:06:27.450 --> 00:06:28.283
- [Mark] Yeah. Strange.

00:06:28.283 --> 00:06:29.280
There's nothing wrong with strange.

00:06:29.280 --> 00:06:30.340
- Nothing wrong with strange.

00:06:30.340 --> 00:06:31.930
I'm more strange than I am weird.

00:06:31.930 --> 00:06:33.490
It just make me feel me.

00:06:33.490 --> 00:06:34.323
I feel like a stranger for myself.

00:06:34.323 --> 00:06:35.450
I'm just gonna separate it.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:36.290
- [Mark] I just find you interesting.

00:06:36.290 --> 00:06:37.530
I see tons of potential in you

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:38.690
but

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:39.523
how we're gonna

00:06:40.420 --> 00:06:43.520
make that turn into something
productive, I don't know.

00:06:43.520 --> 00:06:45.082
Maybe you don't want to.

00:06:45.082 --> 00:06:46.140
- It's not that I don't want to.

00:06:46.140 --> 00:06:48.520
I just have no clue as to,

00:06:48.520 --> 00:06:50.010
there's certain things I wanna go about

00:06:50.010 --> 00:06:51.604
but I feel so separated from them.

00:06:51.604 --> 00:06:53.370
And it's not just 'cause
of living the way I do.

00:06:53.370 --> 00:06:55.150
I just, like you said responsibility.

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:56.640
I have no sense of
responsibility whatsoever.

00:06:56.640 --> 00:06:57.580
I have

00:06:57.580 --> 00:06:59.700
no sense of

00:06:59.700 --> 00:07:01.250
entitlement to anything.

00:07:01.250 --> 00:07:03.380
So it's hard to weigh myself down

00:07:04.950 --> 00:07:06.973
to need things, you know?

00:07:10.360 --> 00:07:11.810
So I guess I don't have that,

00:07:14.221 --> 00:07:16.080
but I do want it, I suppose.

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:18.483
- [Mark] Do you have
any goals for next year?

00:07:19.380 --> 00:07:20.430
New year's resolutions?

00:07:20.430 --> 00:07:21.780
Anything?

00:07:21.780 --> 00:07:25.540
- To be a better witch. (chuckles)

00:07:25.540 --> 00:07:26.747
- To be a better witch.
(Mark laughs)

00:07:26.747 --> 00:07:30.280
- I think 2021's gonna be
very similar to 2020 for you.

00:07:30.280 --> 00:07:31.360
- Yeah.

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:32.770
- 2020 was strange.

00:07:32.770 --> 00:07:35.070
You can think of polarity or duality.

00:07:35.070 --> 00:07:36.980
Like at the beginning of the
year was so intense for me

00:07:36.980 --> 00:07:39.760
and then the end of the
year, it was really calm.

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:42.400
But I just wonder if it means anything.

00:07:42.400 --> 00:07:44.900
Things will just have to
mean something, you know?

00:07:46.446 --> 00:07:47.903
(motorcycle roaring)

00:07:47.903 --> 00:07:48.967
- [Mark] I just want you to be happy.

00:07:48.967 --> 00:07:49.885
And you seem to be happy.

00:07:49.885 --> 00:07:51.080
- I am happy.

00:07:51.080 --> 00:07:52.940
- [Mark] Do you have
moments where you're down?

00:07:52.940 --> 00:07:54.250
- Of course. Who doesn't?

00:07:54.250 --> 00:07:55.083
- [Mark] Yeah. Everybody does.

00:07:55.083 --> 00:07:56.160
No, but you,

00:07:56.160 --> 00:07:57.790
I've only seen you one
time where you were down.

00:07:57.790 --> 00:07:59.330
- But I feel like I know
how to be satisfied.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:01.040
Yeah, that's true.

00:08:01.040 --> 00:08:01.873
I was, yeah.

00:08:01.873 --> 00:08:02.780
I was really out of it that day.

00:08:02.780 --> 00:08:04.630
What was going on that day?

00:08:04.630 --> 00:08:08.320
I just kind of gotten rough about,

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:10.380
so, having that, you know what I mean?

00:08:10.380 --> 00:08:12.380
It wasn't even in Skid Row,
it was really weird part.

00:08:12.380 --> 00:08:13.820
It was an odd, was like
a really nice area.

00:08:13.820 --> 00:08:15.170
- [Mark] No, but get getting
roughed up on the street.

00:08:15.170 --> 00:08:16.600
It's gotta be very disconcerting.

00:08:16.600 --> 00:08:18.660
- Well, disconcerting (chuckles)

00:08:18.660 --> 00:08:20.710
it's a fact of it. Isn't it?

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:23.767
It's supposed to be the
all giving fact of it.

00:08:23.767 --> 00:08:25.700
It's what people wanna see.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:28.350
- [Mark] What's the worst thing
about living on the street?

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:30.300
- I'm suffering.

00:08:30.300 --> 00:08:31.133
Help me.

00:08:31.133 --> 00:08:31.966
You know what I mean?

00:08:31.966 --> 00:08:32.850
Like, (chuckles)

00:08:32.850 --> 00:08:33.683
I don't know.

00:08:33.683 --> 00:08:35.260
- [Mark] Everybody feel sorry for you?

00:08:35.260 --> 00:08:36.110
- Pretension. Yeah.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:38.150
It's not that I mind who have
been feeling sorry for me.

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:42.790
I just mind people feeling
bad for me in an abrasive way.

00:08:42.790 --> 00:08:43.750
Like

00:08:44.860 --> 00:08:47.990
people who give you a
certain sort of attention

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:49.520
It's not just like, what
the fuck are you wearing?

00:08:49.520 --> 00:08:51.900
But let's say, let's
take that as an example.

00:08:51.900 --> 00:08:54.063
Okay. Keep it pushing.

00:08:54.974 --> 00:08:58.340
You will feel really
entitled to a piece of you

